  <h3>{{ user.name }}</h3>
</template>
```

#### v-on / @ - Theory: Event Handling

**Event Flow:**
```
User does something (click, type, etc.)
    ↓
Browser fires event
    ↓
Vue catches it
    ↓
Calls handler method with event object
    ↓
Handler updates data
    ↓
Component re-renders
```

**Event Modifiers - Change Event Behavior:**
```javascript
// Modifiers change HOW Vue handles the event

@submit.prevent
  // Calls e.preventDefault()
  // Prevents form from submitting (page reload)
  
@click.stop
  // Calls e.stopPropagation()
  // Prevents event from bubbling up to parent

@click.self
  // Only triggers if event target is this element
  // Ignores bubbled events from children

@click.once
  // Handler only fires once

@click.capture
  // Uses capture phase instead of bubbling
```

**Key Modifiers - Listen for Specific Keys:**
```javascript
// Keyboard keys
@keyup.enter      // Enter key only
@keydown.escape   // Escape key only
@keyup.space      // Space key only

// Modifier combinations
@keyup.ctrl.a     // Ctrl+A together
@keydown.shift.enter

// Mouse buttons
@click.left       // Left click only
@click.right      // Right click only
@click.middle     // Middle click only
```

```html
