## Routing - Theory: Single Page Applications

### Why Vue Router Exists

Traditional web apps: Each URL = full page reload (slow, flickers)
Single Page App: One HTML file, Vue controls what shows based on URL

**Vue Router Purpose:**
- Map URLs to components
- Update component without page reload
- Maintain browser history (back button works)
- Enable client-side navigation

**How Vue Router Works:**
```
User clicks link
    ↓
Router intercepts (prevents page reload)
    ↓
Changes route in browser URL
    ↓
Vue matches URL to route
    ↓
Loads matching component
    ↓
Renders new component (no page reload!)
    ↓
Browser history updated (back button works)
```

### Vue Router Setup

```bash
npm install vue-router@4
```

```javascript
// router/index.js - Route definitions
import { createRouter, createWebHistory } from 'vue-router'
import Home from '@/pages/Home.vue'
import About from '@/pages/About.vue'
import UserDetail from '@/pages/UserDetail.vue'
import NotFound from '@/pages/NotFound.vue'

// Define routes: URL → Component
const routes = [
  {
    path: '/',                    // URL path
    component: Home,              // Component to show
    name: 'home'                  // Named route (for easy linking)
  },
  {
    path: '/about',
    component: About,
    name: 'about'
  },
  {
    // Dynamic route - :id is parameter
    path: '/users/:id',
    component: UserDetail,
    name: 'user-detail',
    props: true                   // Pass URL params as props
  },
  {
    // Catch-all route - must be last
    path: '/:pathMatch(.*)*',     // Matches anything not matched above
    component: NotFound,
    name: 'not-found'
  }
]

const router = createRouter({
  history: createWebHistory(),    // Use browser history
  routes
})

export default router
```

```javascript
// main.js - Install router
import { createApp } from 'vue'
import App from './App.vue'
import router from './router'

createApp(App).use(router).mount('#app')
```

### Router Components and Hooks

**RouterLink** - Creates navigation links
**RouterView** - Shows matched component
**useRouter()** - Programmatic navigation
**useRoute()** - Access current route info

```vue
<!-- App.vue -->
<template>
  <div>
    <!-- Navigation -->
    <nav>
      <!-- RouterLink instead of <a> (prevents reload) -->
      <RouterLink to="/">Home</RouterLink>
      <RouterLink to="/about">About</RouterLink>
      <!-- Active link gets 'router-link-active' class -->
    </nav>
    
    <!-- Route content goes here -->
    <RouterView />
  </div>
</template>

<script setup>
import { useRouter, useRoute } from 'vue-router'

const router = useRouter()  // For programmatic navigation
const route = useRoute()    // For accessing current route info

// Programmatic navigation (like router.push in Options API)
const navigate = () => {
  router.push({ name: 'about' })  // Navigate by name
  // or
  router.push('/about')            // Navigate by path
}

// Access route params and query
const userId = route.params.id           // /users/123 → id = '123'
const searchQuery = route.query.search   // ?search=vue → 'vue'
</script>
```

### Route Guards - Theory: Protecting Routes

**Why Route Guards Exist:**
- Verify user is logged in before accessing admin page
- Fetch data before showing page
- Prevent unsaved changes
- Redirect based on user role

**Guard Types:**

```javascript
// Global guard - runs on EVERY navigation
router.beforeEach((to, from, next) => {
  // to = destination route
  // from = current route
  // next() = continue, next(false) = cancel, next('/login') = redirect
  
  if (to.requiresAuth && !isLoggedIn) {
    // Destination requires auth but user not logged in
    next('/login')      // Redirect to login
  } else {
    next()              // Allow navigation
  }
})

// Global after guard - runs AFTER navigation complete
router.afterEach((to, from) => {
  // Good for: analytics, progress indicators
  document.title = to.meta.title || 'App'
})

// Per-route guard
const routes = [
  {
    path: '/admin',
    component: Admin,
    beforeEnter: (to, from, next) => {
      // Only runs for this specific route
      if (user.isAdmin) {
        next()
      } else {
        next('/')  // Redirect if not admin
      }
    }
  }
]

// In-component guard
export default {
  beforeRouteLeave(to, from, next) {
    // Called when leaving this component
    if (hasUnsavedChanges) {
      const answer = confirm('Unsaved changes. Leave anyway?')
      next(answer)  // true = leave, false = stay
    } else {
      next()
    }
  }
}
```

### Route Guards
