## Advanced Topics - Theory: Complex Vue Patterns

### Teleport - Theory: Render Anywhere

**Problem Solved:**
```html
<!-- Component deeply nested -->
<div class="page">
  <div class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <Modal>  <!-- Modal here, but CSS is limited by parent -->
        <!-- Modal renders here, constrained by page/section/container -->
        <!-- z-index issues, transform/overflow breaks positioning -->
      </Modal>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Better: Render modal to <body> -->
<Teleport to="body">
  <Modal>  <!-- Renders to <body>, not constrained -->
  </Modal>
</Teleport>
```

**Teleport Purpose:**
- Render component's template to a different DOM node
- Solves z-index and CSS containment issues with modals, tooltips, dropdowns
- Component logic stays where it is, only rendering location changes

```vue
<!-- Component.vue -->
<template>
  <Teleport to="body">
    <div class="modal-overlay">
      <div class="modal">
        <h1>Modal</h1>
        <slot></slot>
        <button @click="close">Close</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Teleport>
</template>

<!-- Usage - component logic here, renders to body -->
<Modal>
  <p>Modal content - logic lives with component, renders to body</p>
</Modal>

<!-- Result in HTML: -->
<!-- 
  <body>
    <div id="app">...</div>
    <div class="modal-overlay">  <!-- Teleported here! -->
      <div class="modal">...</div>
    </div>
  </body>
-->
```

### Suspense - Theory: Async Component Loading

**Problem Without Suspense:**
```vue
<!-- Without Suspense - can't wait for async setup -->
<AsyncComponent />

<!-- Component has async setup() -->
<script setup>
const data = await fetch('/api/data')  // Takes time
</script>

<!-- Problem: Component renders before data loads -->
<!-- Race condition, undefined data, errors -->
```

**Solution With Suspense:**
```vue
<!-- With Suspense - shows loading until ready -->
<Suspense>
  <template #default>
    <AsyncComponent />  <!-- Waits for this to be ready -->
  </template>
  
  <template #fallback>
    <div>Loading...</div>  <!-- Shows until ready -->
  </template>
</Suspense>

<!-- Flow:
  1. Suspense shows fallback
  2. AsyncComponent setup() runs (fetching data)
  3. When ready, replaces fallback with default
  4. No undefined data, clean loading UX -->
```

### Keep-Alive - Theory: Component State Preservation

**Problem Without Keep-Alive:**
```vue
<!-- Without Keep-Alive -->
<component :is="activeComponent" />

<!-- If you switch components A → B → A -->
<!-- A is destroyed, then recreated from scratch -->
<!-- Lost state: form data, scroll position, etc. -->
```

**Solution With Keep-Alive:**
```vue
<!-- With Keep-Alive -->
<KeepAlive>
  <component :is="activeComponent" />
</KeepAlive>

<!-- If you switch components A → B → A -->
<!-- A is cached, not destroyed -->
<!-- State preserved: form data, scroll position, etc. -->

<!-- Performance:
  Without Keep-Alive:
    A → destroy/recreate → A' (slower, state lost)
  
  With Keep-Alive:
    A (cached) → B (showing) → A (restore from cache, instant)
-->
```

**Include/Exclude:**
```vue
<!-- Only cache ComponentA and ComponentB -->
<KeepAlive include="ComponentA,ComponentB">
  <component :is="activeComponent" />
</KeepAlive>

<!-- Cache all except ComponentExpensive -->
<KeepAlive exclude="ComponentExpensive">
  <component :is="activeComponent" />
</KeepAlive>

<!-- Lifecycle with Keep-Alive -->
<script setup>
import { onActivated, onDeactivated } from 'vue'

onActivated(() => {
  // Component shown after being cached
  // Good for: resume timers, restart animations
})

onDeactivated(() => {
  // Component hidden but kept alive
  // Good for: pause timers, save state
})
</script>
```

### Transitions - Theory: Smooth Animations

**Why Transitions Exist:**
- Abrupt element appearance/disappearance is jarring
- Transitions smooth changes for better UX

**Transition Phases:**
```
v-if becomes true
  ↓
Enter phase starts
  ↓
Enter-active: Animate
  ↓
Enter complete
  ↓
Element shown

---

v-if becomes false
  ↓
Leave phase starts
  ↓
Leave-active: Animate
  ↓
Leave complete
  ↓
Element removed
```

```vue
<template>
  <Transition name="fade">
    <div v-if="show">Hello</div>
  </Transition>
</template>

<style scoped>
/* Enter phase: from invisible to visible */
.fade-enter-from {
  opacity: 0;
}

/* During enter animation */
.fade-enter-active {
  transition: opacity 0.5s;
}

/* After enter (final state) */
.fade-enter-to {
  opacity: 1;
}

/* Leave phase: from visible to invisible */
.fade-leave-from {
  opacity: 1;
}

/* During leave animation */
.fade-leave-active {
  transition: opacity 0.5s;
}

/* After leave (final state) */
.fade-leave-to {
  opacity: 0;
}

/* Shorthand: same animation for both */
.fade-enter-active,
.fade-leave-active {
  transition: opacity 0.5s;
}

.fade-enter-from,
.fade-leave-to {
  opacity: 0;
}
```

**Transition Group for Lists:**
