## Best Practices - Theory: Professional Vue Development

### Why Best Practices Matter

Professional Vue development isn't just about making it work - it's about making it:
- **Maintainable:** Others (and future you) can understand it
- **Scalable:** Adding features doesn't become exponentially harder
- **Performant:** Users get fast experiences
- **Testable:** You can verify code works correctly
- **Debuggable:** Finding and fixing bugs is easy

**Bad practices lead to:**
```
Technical Debt
    ↓
Hard to add features
    ↓
More bugs introduced
    ↓
Takes longer to fix
    ↓
Team frustrated
    ↓
Quality suffers
```

**Good practices create:**
```
Clean architecture
    ↓
Easy to add features
    ↓
Fewer bugs
    ↓
Quick fixes
    ↓
Team productive
    ↓
High quality
```

### 1. Component Organization - Theory: Structure for Scale

**Why Organization Matters:**
```
Bad Organization:
  src/
    ├── Button.vue
    ├── Modal.vue
    ├── UserList.vue
    ├── ProductCard.vue
    └── [50 more files scattered]
  
  Problem: 50+ files in one folder, impossible to find anything
  
Good Organization:
  src/
    ├── components/common/      ← Reusable UI pieces
    ├── components/layout/      ← Page structure
    ├── components/features/    ← Feature-specific components
    ├── pages/                  ← Full page components
    ├── composables/            ← Logic reuse
    ├── stores/                 ← Shared state
    └── services/               ← API and business logic
  
  Benefit: Everything has a place, easy to navigate
```

