#### Composition API Computed

```javascript
import { ref, computed } from 'vue'

export default {
  setup() {
    const firstName = ref('John')
    const lastName = ref('Doe')
    
    // Readonly computed
    const fullName = computed(() => {
      console.log('Computing...')
      return firstName.value + ' ' + lastName.value
    })
    
    // Computed with setter
    const editableName = computed({
      get: () => firstName.value + ' ' + lastName.value,
      set: (newValue) => {
        const [first, last] = newValue.split(' ')
        firstName.value = first
        lastName.value = last
      }
    })
    
    return { firstName, lastName, fullName, editableName }
  }
}
```

### Watchers and Effects Deep Dive

#### Watch vs Computed vs WatchEffect

```javascript
// COMPUTED - for derived state
const fullName = computed(() => {
  // Automatically tracks dependencies
  return firstName.value + ' ' + lastName.value
})
// Use: When you need a derived value that updates when dependencies change

// WATCH - for side effects
watch(firstName, (newVal, oldVal) => {
  console.log('First name changed from', oldVal, 'to', newVal)
  // Perform side effects like API calls
})
// Use: When you need to perform actions when specific data changes

// WATCHEFFECT - automatically track dependencies
watchEffect(() => {
  console.log(`${firstName.value} ${lastName.value}`)
  // Runs whenever firstName or lastName changes
})
// Use: When you want automatic dependency tracking
```

#### Practical Watch Examples

```javascript
