### Concept 2: Template Interpolation and Data Binding

#### Theory Explained
Templates are the HTML view layer. Vue provides syntax to bind data to the template and update it reactively.

**Interpolation Flow:**

```
Component Data (JavaScript) → Template Syntax → Rendered HTML
                                    ↓
                              Vue compiles
                                    ↓
                              Watcher installed
                                    ↓
                            Data changes → HTML updates
```

**Text Interpolation - {{ }}**

```html
<!-- Simple: Display data as text -->
<p>{{ message }}</p>
<!-- If message = "Hello", renders: <p>Hello</p> -->

<!-- Expressions: Can perform operations -->
<p>{{ count + 1 }}</p>
<!-- Computed inline: 5 + 1 = 6 -->

<!-- Method calls: Can call methods -->
<p>{{ formatDate(date) }}</p>
<!-- Calls formatDate method with date -->

<!-- Ternary: Conditional expressions -->
<p>{{ isAdmin ? 'Administrator' : 'User' }}</p>
<!-- Shows "Administrator" or "User" based on condition -->

<!-- Array operations: Manipulate data -->
<p>{{ items.filter(i => i.active).length }}</p>
<!-- Shows count of active items -->

<!-- WHY: Interpolation is evaluated every render time
     If you use it in template 5 times, Vue evaluates it 5 times
     Problem: Expensive operations slow down rendering
     Solution: Use computed properties instead
-->

<!-- ❌ BAD: Expensive operation in template -->
<div>{{ heavyCalculation(data) }}</div>
<div>{{ heavyCalculation(data) }}</div>
<div>{{ heavyCalculation(data) }}</div>
<!-- Runs 3 times! -->

<!-- ✅ GOOD: Use computed -->
<!-- Script: const result = computed(() => heavyCalculation(data)) -->
<div>{{ result }}</div>
<div>{{ result }}</div>
<div>{{ result }}</div>
<!-- Computed caches, runs once -->
```

**Attribute Binding - v-bind or :**

```html
<!-- Theory: bind JavaScript value to HTML attribute -->
<!-- Syntax: v-bind:attributeName or :attributeName -->

<!-- Basic attribute -->
<img v-bind:src="imageSrc" />
<!-- If imageSrc = "photo.jpg", renders: <img src="photo.jpg" /> -->

<!-- Dynamic class -->
<div :class="{ active: isActive }">
  <!-- If isActive = true, renders: class="active" -->
  <!-- If isActive = false, renders: class="" -->
</div>

<!-- Why v-bind instead of {{ }}? -->
<!-- {{ }} is for text content, :prop is for attributes -->
<!-- <img src="{{ url }}"> doesn't work - would be literal text -->
<!-- <img :src="url"> works - binds actual URL -->

<!-- Dynamic style -->
<div :style="{ color: activeColor, fontSize: fontSize + 'px' }">
  <!-- Builds inline style dynamically -->
  <!-- If activeColor = 'red', fontSize = 14 -->
  <!-- Renders: style="color: red; font-size: 14px;" -->
</div>

<!-- Boolean attributes - special handling -->
<button :disabled="isLoading">Submit</button>
<!-- If isLoading = true, renders: <button disabled>Submit</button> -->
<!-- If isLoading = false, renders: <button>Submit</button> -->
<!-- Not: <button disabled="false"> - that's invalid HTML -->

<!-- Multiple bindings - v-bind object -->
<div v-bind="attributes"></div>
<!-- If attributes = { id: 'foo', class: 'bar', title: 'baz' } -->
<!-- Renders: <div id="foo" class="bar" title="baz"></div> -->
```

**Why Binding Matters:**

```javascript
// Without Vue - manual updates
document.querySelector('img').src = imageSrc
document.querySelector('img').alt = imageAlt
// If imageSrc changes, you must manually update again

// With Vue - automatic updates
// <img :src="imageSrc" :alt="imageAlt" />
// If imageSrc changes, Vue automatically updates img.src
// Reactive synchronization between data and DOM
```

