### Concept 6: Component Props - Parent to Child Communication

#### Theory Explained
Props are the way parents pass data to children. They're one-way: parent can update, but child cannot (data flows down, not up).

**Props Theory:**

```
Parent Component
    ↓ (passes data)
   Props
    ↓ (child receives)
Child Component
    ↓ (cannot modify back)
Parent stays source of truth
```

**Why Props Are One-Way:**

```javascript
// GOOD: Data flows one way
// Parent.vue
export default {
  setup() {
    const count = ref(0)
    const increment = () => count.value++
    
    return { count, increment }
  }
}

// Template: <Child :count="count" @increment="increment" />

// Child.vue
// Receives count as prop
// Cannot do: count.value++ (violates prop)
// Instead: emit event to parent
// Parent increments count
// New value flows back down as updated prop

// Why one-way?
// Single source of truth: Parent owns data
// Prevents confusion: Parent is responsible for updates
// Easier to debug: Data flows in one direction

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────

// ❌ BAD: Child modifying prop directly
export default {
  props: ['count'],
  methods: {
    increment() {
      this.count++  // 🚨 WRONG - mutates parent's data
      // Parent thinks count is 5
      // Child thinks count is 6
      // Confusion and bugs!
    }
  }
}

// ✅ RIGHT: Child emitting event
export default {
  props: ['count'],
  emits: ['update:count'],
  methods: {
    increment() {
      this.$emit('update:count', this.count + 1)
    }
  }
}

// Parent handles update:
// <Child :count="count" @update:count="(val) => count = val" />
// Or use v-model shorthand:
// <Child v-model="count" />
```

**Prop Validation - Ensuring Correct Data:**

```javascript
// NO VALIDATION (Bad practice)
defineProps(['user'])
// Any data accepted, including wrong types

// TYPE VALIDATION
defineProps({
  user: Object,        // Any object
  count: Number,       // Any number
  active: Boolean,     // Any boolean
  items: Array         // Any array
})

// MULTIPLE TYPES
defineProps({
  count: [String, Number],  // Accepts either string or number
})

// REQUIRED VALIDATION
defineProps({
  id: {
    type: String,
    required: true  // Must be provided, error if missing
  }
})

// DEFAULT VALUE
defineProps({
  status: {
    type: String,
    default: 'pending'  // If not provided, uses 'pending'
  }
})

// CUSTOM VALIDATOR
defineProps({
  priority: {
    type: Number,
    validator(value) {
      // Custom validation logic
      return value >= 1 && value <= 5  // Only 1-5 allowed
    }
  }
})

// Why validate?
// Catch bugs early: Wrong data type → Error in console
// Documentation: Props validator documents expected data
// Runtime safety: Invalid data rejected before use
```

