### Concept 7: Component Events - Child to Parent Communication

#### Theory Explained
Events are how children communicate with parents. Child emits event with data, parent listens and responds. Maintains one-way data flow.

**Events Theory:**

```
Child Component
    ↓ (emits event)
  Event
    ↓ (parent listens)
Parent Component
    ↓ (responds/updates)
New prop value flows to child
```

**Emit Pattern:**

```javascript
// SIMPLE EVENT: Just notification, no data
// Child.vue
const emit = defineEmits(['close'])

const handleClose = () => {
  emit('close')  // Notify parent
}

// Parent template:
// <Modal @close="isModalOpen = false" />
// When child emits 'close', parent closes modal

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────

// EVENT WITH PAYLOAD: Pass data with event
// Child.vue
const emit = defineEmits(['update:count'])

const handleIncrement = () => {
  emit('update:count', newCount)  // Send data to parent
}

// Parent template:
// <Counter :count="count" @update:count="(val) => count = val" />

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────

// EVENT WITH VALIDATION: Ensure correct payload
const emit = defineEmits({
  submit: (payload) => {
    // Validator function
    // Returns true if valid, false if invalid
    return typeof payload === 'object' &&
           'email' in payload &&
           'password' in payload
  }
})

// Parent will get console warning if invalid payload sent

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────

// MULTIPLE EVENTS: Component emits different events
const emit = defineEmits(['save', 'cancel', 'delete'])

const handleSave = (formData) => {
  emit('save', formData)
}

const handleCancel = () => {
  emit('cancel')
}

const handleDelete = (id) => {
  emit('delete', id)
}

// Parent:
// <Form @save="onSave" @cancel="onCancel" @delete="onDelete" />
```

**v-model Pattern - Two-way Binding Shorthand:**

```javascript
// Without v-model:
// <input :value="message" @input="(e) => message = e.target.value" />
// Verbose, hard to read

// With v-model:
// <input v-model="message" />
// Clean and intuitive

// How v-model works internally:
// 1. Binds :modelValue prop
// 2. Listens for @update:modelValue event
// 3. Automatically updates parent data

// For custom component:
// Parent: <MyInput v-model="text" />
// Equivalent to:
// Parent: <MyInput :modelValue="text" @update:modelValue="text = $event" />

// Child component must:
// 1. Accept modelValue prop
// 2. Emit update:modelValue event

// Child.vue with v-model support:
defineProps(['modelValue'])
const emit = defineEmits(['update:modelValue'])

const handleInput = (newValue) => {
  emit('update:modelValue', newValue)
}
```

