### Concept 8: Provide/Inject - Deep Tree Communication

#### Theory Explained
For deeply nested components, passing props through every level (prop drilling) is tedious. Provide/Inject allows any descendant to access data without props.

**Provide/Inject Theory:**

```
Ancestor Component (provides data)
    ↓
Parent Component (doesn't need to know)
    ↓
Child Component (doesn't need to know)
    ↓
Deep Nested Component (injects data directly from ancestor)
```

**Why Provide/Inject?**

```javascript
// ❌ WITHOUT PROVIDE/INJECT: Prop drilling
// App.vue
export default {
  setup() {
    const theme = ref('dark')
    
    return { theme }
  }
}

// Template: <Header :theme="theme" />

// Header.vue (receives but doesn't use)
export default {
  props: ['theme'],
  setup(props) {
    return { theme: props.theme }
  }
}

// Template: <Navbar :theme="theme" />

// Navbar.vue (receives but doesn't use)
export default {
  props: ['theme'],
  setup(props) {
    return { theme: props.theme }
  }
}

// Template: <UserMenu :theme="theme" />

// UserMenu.vue (finally uses it!)
export default {
  props: ['theme'],
  setup(props) {
    // Use theme here
    const backgroundColor = props.theme === 'dark' ? '#333' : '#fff'
  }
}

// Problem: Header and Navbar components don't use theme
// But they must pass it through (prop drilling)
// Tedious to maintain

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────

// ✅ WITH PROVIDE/INJECT: Direct injection

// App.vue (provides)
export default {
  setup() {
    const theme = ref('dark')
    provide('theme', theme)  // Make available to all descendants
    
    return { theme }
  }
}

// Header.vue (no props needed)
export default {
  setup() {
    // No props, no drilling
    return {}
  }
}

// Navbar.vue (no props needed)
export default {
  setup() {
    // No props, no drilling
    return {}
  }
}

// UserMenu.vue (injects directly)
export default {
  setup() {
    const theme = inject('theme')  // Get from App directly
    const backgroundColor = theme.value === 'dark' ? '#333' : '#fff'
    return { backgroundColor }
  }
}

// Benefits:
// - No prop drilling through intermediate components
// - Cleaner code
// - Easier to maintain
// - Intermediate components don't need to know about theme
```

**Provide/Inject with Reactivity:**

```javascript
// SHARING REACTIVE DATA
// Parent.vue
export default {
  setup() {
    const isDarkMode = ref(false)
    
    provide('isDarkMode', isDarkMode)  // Provide ref
    // Descendants get the ref, not the value
    // When ref changes, all descendants see the change
  }
}

// Child.vue
export default {
  setup() {
    const isDarkMode = inject('isDarkMode')
    
    // isDarkMode is a ref
    console.log(isDarkMode.value)  // Access with .value
    
    // When parent changes isDarkMode:
    watch(isDarkMode, (newVal) => {
      applyTheme(newVal)
    })
  }
}

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────

// SHARING METHODS
// Parent.vue
export default {
  setup() {
    const toggleTheme = () => {
      isDarkMode.value = !isDarkMode.value
    }
    
    provide('toggleTheme', toggleTheme)
  }
}

// Child.vue
export default {
  setup() {
    const toggleTheme = inject('toggleTheme')
    
    return { toggleTheme }
  }
}

// Template: <button @click="toggleTheme">Toggle Theme</button>
```

