### Concept 10: Lifecycle and Component Timing

#### Theory Explained
Components have different lifecycle stages. Vue runs hooks at each stage to let you execute code at the right time.

**Lifecycle Stages - When to Use Each:**

```javascript
// STAGE 1: CREATION (data and methods ready, DOM not)
beforeCreate() {
  // Almost never used
  // data() not ready yet
}

created() {
  // Data ready, methods ready
  // DOM not ready yet
  // Use for: Initialize data, fetch data that doesn't need DOM
  this.user = fetch('/api/user')
  this.setupListeners()
}

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────

// STAGE 2: MOUNTING (adding to DOM)
beforeMount() {
  // Component ready to mount
  // Last chance to modify before DOM
  // Rarely used
}

mounted() {
  // Component now in DOM
  // Can access DOM refs, initialize DOM libraries
  // Use for: DOM initialization, scroll listeners, autofocus
  this.$refs.input.focus()
  initializeChart(this.$refs.chartContainer)
  window.addEventListener('scroll', this.handleScroll)
}

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────

// STAGE 3: UPDATING (when data changes)
beforeUpdate() {
  // Data changed, DOM not updated yet
  // Rare use case: save DOM state
  this.scrollPosition = window.scrollY
}

updated() {
  // Data changed, DOM updated
  // Use for: React to DOM changes
  this.scrollTo(this.scrollPosition)
}

// ─────────────────────────────────────────────

// STAGE 4: UNMOUNTING (removing from DOM)
beforeUnmount() {
  // About to be destroyed
  // Clean up external resources
  // Use for: Remove listeners, cancel requests
  window.removeEventListener('scroll', this.handleScroll)
}

unmounted() {
  // Completely removed
  // Final cleanup
  this.cancelPendingRequests()
}
```

**Common Lifecycle Patterns:**

```javascript
// PATTERN 1: Fetch data on mount
export default {
  data() {
    return { user: null }
  },
  async mounted() {
    this.user = await fetchUser()
  }
}

// PATTERN 2: Cleanup listeners
export default {
  mounted() {
    window.addEventListener('resize', this.handleResize)
  },
  unmounted() {
    window.removeEventListener('resize', this.handleResize)
  }
}

